      AI and computational methods for spatial analysis
      New data and inference techniques treated as research objects in their own right: their capabilities, failure modes and responsible deployment.





      Exclusion and spatial inequality in housing markets
      How housing markets exclude, by prejudice, gatekeeping or scarcity, and how spatial constraints turn individual decisions into population-level inequality.





      Spatial personality
      Estimating Big Five personality at scale from digital traces, and mapping how regional personality shapes entrepreneurship, mobility and resilience.





      Spatial analysis of environment and climate
      Spatial measurement where official statistics are thin, and whether environmental commitments survive contact with incentives.





      Spatial analysis of real estate and finance
      Extracting reliable price signals from thin, irregularly traded stock, and asking what actually moves property values.





      Behavioural economics of housing decisions
      Why households depart from textbook-rational behaviour in housing decisions, and what reference dependence and loss aversion mean for policy.





      Land use policy in China
      China&#039;s distinctive rural and urban land regimes, and their consequences for inequality, environmental quality and productivity.




Research Grants
I currently lead four externally funded projects, each in partnership with co-investigators overseas. Each page below sets out the project, the team, and the publications and working papers it supports.

